  "scientific_definitions_and_notes": {
    "methodology_scope": "Exploratory flood exposure and geographic proximity analysis. Calculates planar Euclidean distance (EPSG:32646) from mapped healthcare facility points to the nearest boundary of the satellite-detected flood polygon layer.",
    "water_classification_rigor": "UNOSAT Product 3954 explicitly isolates 'Flood Water' with status 'New Water / Water Increase'. Permanent river channels and baseline reference water bodies are not classified as flood inundation.",
    "accessibility_distinction": "Straight-line Euclidean proximity does NOT represent actual road network travel accessibility, travel time, flood water depth, velocity, or operational facility status during the disaster.",
    "temporal_clarity": "Primary analyzed flood extent represents UNOSAT Sentinel-1 observations from the first satellite observation period (18\u201326 August 2024). Both observation periods were computed independently without cross-temporal aggregation.",
    "osm_status_limitation": "OpenStreetMap facility points reflect mapped crowdsourced records and are not field-verified operational facilities as of August 2024.",
    "cartographic_buffer_note": "Visualization buffer rings displayed on Map 3 (500m and 1,000m) are generalized for cartographic rendering (filtered <1,000 m\u00b2 speckle, simplified by 25m). All quantitative proximity metrics in results.csv and summary.json were calculated on the exact original unsimplified analytical geometries.",
